  "cameraHelp1": "Point the back camera at a wall, a picture, a shelf or a door. Hold the phone upright, facing the wall squarely.",
  "cameraHelp2": "Solid lines follow gravity: they are always truly level and plumb. Dashed lines are fixed to your phone, and the small arc between them shows how far it is tilted. The true lines turn orange when the phone is level.",
  "cameraHelp3": "To check an object, tap Freeze, then drag the two orange handles onto one of its edges, like the top of a frame. It shows how far that edge is off level and which side to lift, even if your hand wasn’t level. Drag the line upright to check a plumb edge.",
  "cameraHelp4": "The two buttons at the top show or hide the phone lines and the true lines. The light helps in dark corners; Resume goes back to the live picture.",
  "cameraTip": "For an exact edge reading, face the wall squarely (Forward/back under 5°) and measure near the middle of the picture, where the lens bends lines least. Uses the Level’s on-edge calibration. The picture is never recorded, saved or sent.",
  "cameraAllowTitle": "Allow the camera",
  "cameraAllowBody": "The camera level draws level lines over the camera’s picture and measures edges in it. The picture stays on your phone and is never recorded, saved or sent.",
